JVM Process
A running instance of the Java Virtual Machine that executes Java bytecode and provides the runtime environment for a Java application.

JVM Runtime Memory
The runtime memory areas defined/used by the JVM to execute Java programs and manage application state.


Heap
The runtime data area from which memory for class instances and arrays is allocated; it is shared among JVM threads and is the primary area managed by garbage collection.


Metaspace
A JVM memory area that stores class metadata and related runtime information for loaded classes; it uses native memory rather than the Java Heap.


Java Stack
Each JVM thread has a private JVM stack that stores stack frames for method invocations.


PC Register
Each JVM thread has a private program counter (PC) register) that indicates the address of the JVM instruction currently being executed by that thread.

Native Method Stack
A per-thread memory area used to support execution of native methods, typically methods implemented outside Java, such as through JNI.


Garbage Collector
A JVM subsystem that automatically identifies objects that are no longer reachable and reclaims the Heap memory occupied by them.

